      {
        "symbol": "COL4A2",
        "pmid": "42856351",
        "confidence": 1.0,
        "gwasTraits": [
          "ICH-non-lobar",
          "SVS"
        ],
        "proteinName": "Collagen type IV alpha 2 chain",
        "mendelianRandomization": false,
        "omicsEvidence": [],
        "causalEvidenceSummary": "Established monogenic cSVD gene (Gould syndrome). This paper presents new functional data: Col4a2+/G646D mice, which develop spontaneous ICH, show age-dependent loss of myogenic tone in pial arteries. The mechanism is PKA-dependent RyR2 cluster enlargement, which raises Ca2+ spark and BK channel activity; PKA inhibition rescues it. The human GWAS links to lacunar stroke and deep ICH are background citations.",
        "sourceQuote": "These findings identify age-dependent, PKA-mediated nanoscale remodeling of RyR2 clusters as a central mechanism of cerebrovascular dysfunction in cSVDs associated with mutant COL4A2.",
        "citationOnly": false
